[06/08/26 14:28:05] INFO     Transcription:  For two consecutive     base.py:98
                             numbers, let the first be n. The next             
                             consecutive number is always n plus 1.            
                             Their sum is n plus n plus 1, which               
                             equals 2n plus 1. We say a number is              
                             even when it is a multiple of 2. So 2n            
                             is always even. Adding 1 to any even              
                             number always gives an odd number.                
                             Therefore, the sum of any two                     
                             consecutive numbers is always odd. This           
                             is not a coincidence. It is proved for            
                             all values of n at once.                          
